WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:03.670
-Our first guest is a
Tony-winning and Oscar-nominated

00:00:03.670 --> 00:00:07.606
actor who stars in the new
movie, "The Eyes of Tammy Faye."

00:00:07.606 --> 00:00:09.709
You guys have to see this.
It's amazing.

00:00:09.709 --> 00:00:11.244
It is in theaters this Friday.

00:00:11.244 --> 00:00:14.146
Please welcome Andrew Garfield,
ladies and gentlemen.

00:00:14.146 --> 00:00:15.314
That's my man.

00:00:15.314 --> 00:00:17.016
That's what I'm
talking about, buddy.

00:00:17.016 --> 00:00:19.452
Yes. Oh, my gosh.

00:00:19.452 --> 00:00:21.187
You are great
in this movie, buddy.

00:00:21.187 --> 00:00:23.089
I want to talk about it.

00:00:23.089 --> 00:00:25.091
It's good to see you.
How you doing?

00:00:25.091 --> 00:00:26.292
-It's good to see you, too.

00:00:26.292 --> 00:00:28.761
Very, very happy to be here

00:00:28.761 --> 00:00:30.730
but truly wish I could
be there in person.

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:33.800
I'm in Calgary, a little bit
stuck here doing a show,

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.601
but lovely to be able
to talk to you.

00:00:35.601 --> 00:00:36.902
How are you?
-I'm good.

00:00:36.902 --> 00:00:39.072
I appreciate you coming
on the show, as we all do.

00:00:39.072 --> 00:00:40.740
Yeah, we --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:42.608
Wait till you see.
We have an audience.

00:00:42.608 --> 00:00:44.076
We're coming back, buddy.

00:00:44.076 --> 00:00:45.779
Anyways, a seat's always open --
-I feel it.

00:00:45.779 --> 00:00:47.179
-Seat's always open for you.

00:00:47.179 --> 00:00:49.982
We have -- It's Broadway week
here on our show, and --

00:00:49.982 --> 00:00:51.384
-Whoo!
-Yeah.

00:00:51.384 --> 00:00:55.187
We are honoring, yeah, a bunch
of amazing Broadway shows.

00:00:55.187 --> 00:00:56.890
And you are a Tony winner.

00:00:56.890 --> 00:00:59.124
I -- Absolutely.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:59.124 --> 00:01:02.228
You know the stage pretty well.

00:01:02.228 --> 00:01:04.030
You know anything can happen
in live theater.

00:01:04.030 --> 00:01:06.432
Did anything ever happen to you
during a live performance

00:01:06.432 --> 00:01:07.833
where there was a mess-up
where you're like,

00:01:07.833 --> 00:01:10.202
"Oh, this is going to be tough
to work through"?

00:01:10.202 --> 00:01:14.874
-[ Laughs ] My -- My butt
was facing the audience

00:01:14.874 --> 00:01:20.179
for a prolonged period of time
during "Angels in America."

00:01:20.179 --> 00:01:23.416
It was -- I'm in the middle
of a fight with an angel.

00:01:23.416 --> 00:01:25.484
And if you know the show,
that makes sense.

00:01:25.484 --> 00:01:27.052
If you don't,
it's going to sound odd.

00:01:27.052 --> 00:01:29.622
But I'm in, like, hospital
kind of garments,

00:01:29.622 --> 00:01:33.359
and I'm about to be hoisted up
on a harness

00:01:33.359 --> 00:01:35.127
with this angel
into the rafters.

00:01:35.127 --> 00:01:37.430
And me and the angel
are wrestling.

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:38.964
I've got my arms
around her waist,

00:01:38.964 --> 00:01:40.767
and we're kind of,
like, pretending

00:01:40.767 --> 00:01:42.035
that we're going to wrestle.

00:01:42.035 --> 00:01:44.403
And then we give the guys
in the wings the go-ahead,

00:01:44.403 --> 00:01:45.772
like, "We're ready to go."

00:01:45.772 --> 00:01:47.841
I've got my hands in the loops.
We're ready to go up.

00:01:47.841 --> 00:01:50.443
And we give them the sign,
and, like,

00:01:50.443 --> 00:01:53.913
it feels like 89 minutes passes,

00:01:53.913 --> 00:01:56.248
and we're just, like,
pretending to wrestle

00:01:56.248 --> 00:01:58.183
and like, "Why aren't we
going into the air?"

00:01:58.183 --> 00:02:00.753
-And your -- your butt
is facing the audience?

00:02:00.753 --> 00:02:03.322
-My butt is fully just --

00:02:03.322 --> 00:02:04.724
Just giving full face

00:02:04.724 --> 00:02:06.492
to the crowd.
-Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:02:06.492 --> 00:02:08.795
So, you're pretending
to struggle, fight,

00:02:08.795 --> 00:02:10.496
but nothing's happening?
-Yeah.

00:02:10.496 --> 00:02:12.298
And nothing's happening.

00:02:12.298 --> 00:02:16.669
And my -- my pancake ass
is just, like,

00:02:16.669 --> 00:02:18.037
on full display.

00:02:18.037 --> 00:02:20.439
And -- And the guys
in the wings --

00:02:20.439 --> 00:02:22.542
The guys in the wings are like,
"It's just not --

00:02:22.542 --> 00:02:24.243
I don't know how.
It's just not working."

00:02:24.243 --> 00:02:26.145
And we're like this.
So I'm like what do we do?

00:02:26.145 --> 00:02:28.981
Do we just keep wrestling
with my butt facing everybody?

00:02:28.981 --> 00:02:30.616
And I-I guess
that's what we did.

00:02:30.616 --> 00:02:33.153
Until -- And this is where
it gets really awkward.

00:02:33.153 --> 00:02:36.456
The stage -- The stage manager
walks out

00:02:36.456 --> 00:02:38.891
under this really dramatic music
that's happening,

00:02:38.891 --> 00:02:40.092
with a microphone.

00:02:40.092 --> 00:02:42.628
And he's like, "Um --"
It was a British guy.

00:02:42.628 --> 00:02:44.963
He's like, "Um, so sorry,
ladies and gentlemen,

00:02:44.963 --> 00:02:46.966
but we're having some
technical difficulties.

00:02:46.966 --> 00:02:48.468
We're going to have to
take a pause."

00:02:48.468 --> 00:02:50.736
And meanwhile, like,
me and this actress, Mandy,

00:02:50.736 --> 00:02:52.472
were just, like,
still wrestling.

00:02:52.472 --> 00:02:53.839
[ Laughter ]

00:02:53.839 --> 00:02:55.941
And he stood right next to us.

00:02:55.941 --> 00:02:59.345
And then the curtain comes down
in front of my ass.

00:02:59.345 --> 00:03:00.479
[ Laughter ]

00:03:00.479 --> 00:03:03.048
And then, like, literally,
like, I'm like --

00:03:03.048 --> 00:03:06.286
I'm like, "What do we do? How do
we -- How do we keep the --

00:03:06.286 --> 00:03:08.855
Like, when we figure out
this technical thing,

00:03:08.855 --> 00:03:10.389
how do we start the show again?"

00:03:10.389 --> 00:03:12.558
And I was like,
"I've got an idea!

00:03:12.558 --> 00:03:14.327
Let me put my ass
to the audience,

00:03:14.327 --> 00:03:15.962
and as soon
as the curtain comes up,

00:03:15.962 --> 00:03:18.264
just send me up
on the God damn rig."

00:03:18.264 --> 00:03:22.501
Like, we picked up
exactly where we left off.

00:03:22.501 --> 00:03:24.336
-That's the best, dude.

00:03:24.336 --> 00:03:26.072
What else can you do?

00:03:26.139 --> 00:03:28.207
-What else can you do?
-What else can you do?

00:03:28.207 --> 00:03:30.276
I have -- I have
a couple questions.

00:03:30.276 --> 00:03:32.211
First of all,
you look like a stud

00:03:32.211 --> 00:03:33.546
on the cover of "Variety" here.

00:03:33.546 --> 00:03:34.780
Hey, not too shabby.

00:03:34.780 --> 00:03:36.515
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:36.515 --> 00:03:40.520
I want to -- There's a photo
going around on the Internet

00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:45.892
